<title>SINGAPORE: Pertamina to restart Balongan cracker late week.</title>
<headline>Pertamina to restart Balongan cracker late week.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state-owned oil company Pertamina has failed on February 13 to restart its 83,000 barrels-per-day (bpd) Balongan cracker and will attempt to restart the unit later this week, sources close to the refinery said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The long residue catalytic cracker (RFCC) was shutdown on February 6 for unscheduled repair works and Pertamina was due to restart the unit on February 13.</p>
<p>The source said Pertamina was unable to restart the unit after several attempts and will try again sometime later this week.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
</text>
